.nh
.TH "PB-PORT-NAME" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-port-name - Name machine ports for browser addresses


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb port name [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Give a machine port a name: <name>\&.<machine>\&.<domain> then opens that port in a
browser on every computer of everyone allowed that port. A name never grants access.
--machine names one machine's port (machine managers). --all-machines names that port
on every machine of the active workspace (owners and admins); a machine name of the
same label wins. --top-level --machine makes <name>\&.<domain> open that machine's port
(owners and admins); a machine with that name wins, and pb port name list shows the
top-level name as shadowed. Numeric labels always mean the port.

.PP
With --json, this command group lists its available commands.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for name


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-port(1)\fP, \fBpb-port-name-list(1)\fP, \fBpb-port-name-set(1)\fP, \fBpb-port-name-unset(1)\fP
